<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Rise of the Dominion of Magic

''The public shape:'' a magiocracy grown from Byzantium — the largest of Neo-Thracia's
subservient city-states — where the survivors' cabal ''took over the local Wizard University''
and stood up the Empire's successor state. Four hundred years of tightening grip, hardened by
conflict with the Lich Imperator, Grell raids off the Astral Sea, and Unseelie incursions.
Tactics center ''magic and automatons over trained-fighting troops''; the city's magitech rides
tightly controlled. Southern holdings anchor at ''Tharsis'' and ''the Prismatic University'' in
the Summerlands; sky-castles patrol the annexed city-states the Dominion took the day the
League declared itself. Technomagic mana-supremacists, by the League's reading — and the
League's border defines them as much as their own.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-sealed-spine>>

!! The Sealed Spine (kapu — Session 1.0 intent)

''The Rise began with a question about death.'' ''Umvald'' — a soul of the human-folk
heritages, searching for answers to their mortality — ''reached out into the void… and the
void answered'', because something in the Oort dark had spent aeons straining to see the inner
system and had finally been ''seen back''. The reaching gave the Pale Emperor his vector home
(operator canon, Josh & Freyja, 2026-08-15 — welds to `concepts/the-necrospire`, where the
public meme leaves the cause sealed).

''The rest stands unsealed in the campaign record'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/salt-stair-booth`
#shadowtalk-unsealed): the "eternal life" ruse · Eris's crew tipping Umvald before the altar ·
''the hijacked rite'' · the blood-magic fallout whose survivors became the world's Deathless ·
the cabal taking Byzantium and institutionalizing stolen divinity into a civil service. ''The
Dominion of Magic stands as Umvald's puppet-state'' — the Vampire Lord governing patient as
paperwork, while his old creditor crawls south through the passes with armies.

''The referee's iron:'' the Dominion's origin holds the campaign's moral weight — it began not
in ambition but in ''grief asking the wrong door for help''. Every Deathless citizen of
Byzantium descends from one soul's honest question about mortality, answered by the worst
possible correspondent. Play the Dominion's agents accordingly: true believers in a state built
on an answer their founder knows was a lie.

<<~/ahu>>

